gnóstico.", "DOLOR DE CABEZA:El dolor de cabeza es uno de los síntomas que pueden presentarse en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson, especialmente en etapas avanzadas.", "TEMBLORES:Los temblores son un síntoma neurológico que puede manifestarse en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson debido a la acumulación de cobre.", "DIFICULTAD DE COORDINACIÓN:La dificultad de coordinación es un síntoma neurológico que puede presentarse en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson.", "ABORTOS ESPONTÁNEOS:Los abortos espontáneos repetidos e inexplicables son síntomas que pueden presentarse en mujeres premenopáusicas con Enfermedad de Wilson.", "FATIGA:La fatiga es uno de los primeros síntomas que pueden aparecer en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson.)<|COMPLETE|>", "EW:EW refers to Wilson's disease, a genetic disorder characterized by excessive copper accumulation in the body, which primarily affects the liver and brain. This condition necessitates treatment to manage the copper levels and may ultimately require liver transplantation in severe cases.", "D-PENICILAMINA:D-Penicillamine is a chelating agent and a pharmaceutical treatment primarily used in the management of Wilson's disease, a genetic disorder that leads to excessive copper accumulation in the body. It functions by helping to eliminate excess copper, thereby reducing its levels in the body. D-Penicillamine is considered a first-line medication for this condition, effectively aiding in the treatment and management of copper toxicity associated with Wilson's disease.", "TRIENTINA:Trientina, also known as Trientine, is a medication utilized as an alternative treatment for Wilson's disease, a genetic disorder that leads to excessive accumulation of copper in the body. It functions as a chelator, effectively binding to excess copper and facilitating its removal from the body. Trientine is often noted for being better tolerated than D-Penicillamine, another chelating agent used in the treatment of Wilson's disease. Overall, Trientina serves as a valuable option for managing this condition by helping to reduce copper levels and mitigate its associated health risks.", "HEPATITIS AUTOINMUNE:Autoimmune hepatitis is a condition that can be confused with Wilson's disease, requiring careful diagnosis.", "FAMILIARES DE PRIMER GRADO:First-degree relatives are family members of a patient diagnosed with Wilson's disease (EW) who should be evaluated for the condition due to genetic factors.", "INSUFICIENCIA HEPÁTICA AGUDA:\"INSUFICIENCIA HEPÁTICA AGUDA,\" or acute liver failure, is a critical and severe condition that can arise in patients suffering from Wilson's disease. This medical emergency necessitates immediate intervention to address the potentially life-threatening complications associated with the condition.", "CUPRURIA:Cupruria refers to the presence of excess copper in urine, which is a diagnostic indicator for Wilson's disease (EW).", "KAYSER-FLEISCHER RINGS:Kayser-Fleischer rings are deposits of copper in the cornea, often seen in patients with Wilson's disease, detectable by slit lamp examination.", "ACANTOSIS NIGRICANS:Acanthosis nigricans is a skin condition that may be associated with Wilson's disease, characterized by dark, velvety patches."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}